00:38:21.060 --> 00:38:23.780
ROHINI CHAKRAVARTHY: Hi, my
name is Rohini Chakravarthy

00:38:23.780 --> 00:38:25.160
I'm a first year Sloan student.

00:38:25.160 --> 00:38:28.370
And I will go with a brief
overview of the business

00:38:28.370 --> 00:38:29.700
plan for SiliconTest.

00:38:29.700 --> 00:38:31.700
It will be briefer than
the 10 minutes allotted,

00:38:31.700 --> 00:38:34.240
so we can get to
the winners quicker.

00:38:37.350 --> 00:38:39.210
Let's start with a
challenge statement.

00:38:39.210 --> 00:38:41.540
SEMATECH, which is a
semiconductor industry

00:38:41.540 --> 00:38:45.710
consortium, has articulated
in its National Semiconductor

00:38:45.710 --> 00:38:48.470
technology roadmap that
over the next eight years,

00:38:48.470 --> 00:38:50.210
high frequency
[INAUDIBLE] probes

00:38:50.210 --> 00:38:52.250
will be a major roadblock.

00:38:52.250 --> 00:38:56.360
SiliconTest plans to address
this challenge squarely.

00:38:56.360 --> 00:38:59.120
The company was founded
in February 1998

00:38:59.120 --> 00:39:02.990
and has its roots in
our CEO's graduate work.

00:39:02.990 --> 00:39:05.600
We plan to provide probe
cards for chip testing

00:39:05.600 --> 00:39:08.540
based on new technology
that's more scalable and more

00:39:08.540 --> 00:39:11.210
cost effective than
those currently used.

00:39:11.210 --> 00:39:13.820
To give you a brief
idea, basically chips

00:39:13.820 --> 00:39:15.620
are made on silicon wafers.

00:39:15.620 --> 00:39:17.180
And while they're
still on a wafer,

00:39:17.180 --> 00:39:19.580
a probe card sits on
them, and you test

00:39:19.580 --> 00:39:21.360
each chip for functionality.

00:39:21.360 --> 00:39:25.220
So we plan to make new
kinds of probe cards.

00:39:25.220 --> 00:39:29.430
The company, Arvind Purushotham
is the President and CEO.

00:39:29.430 --> 00:39:32.480
He is currently working
for a large semiconductor

00:39:32.480 --> 00:39:33.920
manufacturer.

00:39:33.920 --> 00:39:36.890
I will be the VP of Marketing
and Sales, and as I said,

00:39:36.890 --> 00:39:39.055
I'm a first year Sloan
student right now.

00:39:39.055 --> 00:39:41.180
We also have William Huffman
who is not here today,

00:39:41.180 --> 00:39:43.250
but he will be the
VP of Engineering.

00:39:43.250 --> 00:39:46.490
And he is an expert in
testing and packaging

00:39:46.490 --> 00:39:49.190
and has worked in the
area for 14 years now.

00:39:49.190 --> 00:39:51.800
We also have two future
recruits who have committed

00:39:51.800 --> 00:39:55.460
to join us pending funding.

00:39:55.460 --> 00:39:57.485
The market opportunity
itself is--

00:39:57.485 --> 00:40:00.320
it's a large market,
450 million as assessed

00:40:00.320 --> 00:40:03.230
by [INAUDIBLE]
research for 1997.

00:40:03.230 --> 00:40:05.570
And it's set to grow
at 25% following

00:40:05.570 --> 00:40:07.250
the growth of the
[? IC ?] market

00:40:07.250 --> 00:40:09.680
at least over the
next few years.

00:40:09.680 --> 00:40:12.620
The industry is characterized
by tight customer and supplier

00:40:12.620 --> 00:40:13.760
relationships.

00:40:13.760 --> 00:40:16.790
Basically, what happens is every
time a new chip is designed,

00:40:16.790 --> 00:40:19.430
a probe card has to be custom
designed to go with it.

00:40:19.430 --> 00:40:22.370
And so the semiconductor
manufacturer and the probe card

00:40:22.370 --> 00:40:25.520
manufacturer act as partners
in developing this probe card.

00:40:25.520 --> 00:40:27.530
So the relationships
have to be really tight

00:40:27.530 --> 00:40:29.998
as you work with the customer.

00:40:29.998 --> 00:40:31.040
It's a fragmented market.

00:40:31.040 --> 00:40:32.870
There are many
important players,

00:40:32.870 --> 00:40:36.450
but no one player holds the
majority of the market share.

00:40:36.450 --> 00:40:40.130
And all of them seem to use
precision machining based

00:40:40.130 --> 00:40:40.800
technology.

00:40:40.800 --> 00:40:44.630
So the underlying technology
is fairly homogeneous.

00:40:44.630 --> 00:40:47.060
The major customers are
semiconductor manufacturers

00:40:47.060 --> 00:40:50.310
here in the US, in Japan,
and in Southeast Asia.

00:40:50.310 --> 00:40:57.840
So examples would be Intel, AMD,
Motorola, Lucent, and so on.

00:40:57.840 --> 00:40:59.610
So to start off
with this venture,

00:40:59.610 --> 00:41:03.030
we plan to request
funding in stages.

00:41:03.030 --> 00:41:06.020
The first milestone will
be a prototype development

00:41:06.020 --> 00:41:07.040
milestone.

00:41:07.040 --> 00:41:11.120
And optimistically speaking,
we will need about 1.3 million

00:41:11.120 --> 00:41:12.950
to achieve this milestone.

00:41:12.950 --> 00:41:16.340
We also believe we will need
an additional 1.5 million

00:41:16.340 --> 00:41:20.810
at least to reach the first
customer acquisition milestone.

00:41:20.810 --> 00:41:25.010
So who are the logical
investors for such a venture?

00:41:25.010 --> 00:41:27.920
It's not uncommon in this
industry for semiconductor

00:41:27.920 --> 00:41:31.400
manufacturers to take equity
positions in key suppliers

00:41:31.400 --> 00:41:33.500
since they invest so
much time in developing

00:41:33.500 --> 00:41:35.130
these relationships.

00:41:35.130 --> 00:41:37.160
So we will look
at those customers

00:41:37.160 --> 00:41:39.340
as possible investors.

00:41:39.340 --> 00:41:41.780
Also, industry associations
that are a possibility.

00:41:41.780 --> 00:41:43.520
SEMATECH, for
example, although they

00:41:43.520 --> 00:41:47.090
don't take equity
positions, do offer

00:41:47.090 --> 00:41:48.710
technical and
financial assistance

00:41:48.710 --> 00:41:53.660
to startups that show
industry changing potential.

00:41:53.660 --> 00:41:56.180
And finally, angel investors
and seed venture capitalists

00:41:56.180 --> 00:41:57.950
will be valuable
sources of funding.

00:41:57.950 --> 00:42:00.410
They will bring in financial
assistance, as well

00:42:00.410 --> 00:42:02.010
as their networks
within the industry,

00:42:02.010 --> 00:42:06.770
and we look at them as very
positive sources of funding.

00:42:06.770 --> 00:42:09.900
So why do I believe SiliconTest
is a great investment?

00:42:09.900 --> 00:42:12.645
We have a very clearly
identified market need.

00:42:12.645 --> 00:42:14.270
We believe we have
the right technology

00:42:14.270 --> 00:42:17.210
and that this is the
right time to deploy it.

00:42:17.210 --> 00:42:19.160
We have assembled a
uniquely qualified set

00:42:19.160 --> 00:42:21.710
of people, people who
understand both the technology

00:42:21.710 --> 00:42:23.840
and the customer environment.

00:42:23.840 --> 00:42:26.510
And through our contacts,
we have unusual access

00:42:26.510 --> 00:42:29.270
to the customer, to
the first customer.

00:42:29.270 --> 00:42:32.300
Finally, we believe we have
a huge upside potential.

00:42:32.300 --> 00:42:33.890
It's a great market.

00:42:33.890 --> 00:42:35.240
It's waiting to change.

00:42:35.240 --> 00:42:36.740
And we believe we can change it.

00:42:36.740 --> 00:42:37.240
Thank you.

