01:09:51.132 --> 01:09:53.340
Let me tell you what the
mission of content providers

01:09:53.340 --> 01:09:55.050
is on the internet.

01:09:55.050 --> 01:09:57.960
Content providers have a
very, very simple mission.

01:09:57.960 --> 01:10:02.160
They want to attract
people to their sites,

01:10:02.160 --> 01:10:04.740
and they want to
keep them there.

01:10:04.740 --> 01:10:07.380
In order to do this, there
are some very simple things

01:10:07.380 --> 01:10:08.160
that they need.

01:10:08.160 --> 01:10:10.740
They need fast, easy,
and reliable access

01:10:10.740 --> 01:10:13.440
to their sites for the clients.

01:10:13.440 --> 01:10:15.180
They also need
personalized content.

01:10:15.180 --> 01:10:19.080
Personalized content allows
these content providers

01:10:19.080 --> 01:10:22.320
to make the user experience
unique for every single person

01:10:22.320 --> 01:10:24.450
who makes it to the site.

01:10:24.450 --> 01:10:27.480
In order to do that, they use
fancy graphics, multimedia,

01:10:27.480 --> 01:10:29.490
and a variety of other
bells and whistles.

01:10:29.490 --> 01:10:31.500
But there is a problem today.

01:10:31.500 --> 01:10:33.390
The problem is that
the ISPs is who

01:10:33.390 --> 01:10:36.000
hosts this content
can't give the content

01:10:36.000 --> 01:10:39.750
providers the quality of service
that they are looking for.

01:10:39.750 --> 01:10:41.760
This results in a
phenomenon known widely

01:10:41.760 --> 01:10:44.860
as the worldwide weight.

01:10:44.860 --> 01:10:47.910
There are a couple of sources
of the worldwide weight.

01:10:47.910 --> 01:10:49.020
One is flash crowds.

01:10:49.020 --> 01:10:50.520
People get to a
site on the internet

01:10:50.520 --> 01:10:52.740
because there's something
exciting going on there.

01:10:52.740 --> 01:10:54.300
The Monica Lewinsky
story breaks.

01:10:54.300 --> 01:10:57.051
Everybody floods cnn.com.

01:10:57.051 --> 01:10:59.040
When this happens,
the content becomes

01:10:59.040 --> 01:11:02.520
phenomenally popular,
the servers are swamped,

01:11:02.520 --> 01:11:04.080
as is the network.

01:11:04.080 --> 01:11:06.060
This can cause such
significant loading

01:11:06.060 --> 01:11:07.920
that the network will
actually go down,

01:11:07.920 --> 01:11:11.310
and nobody gets access
to this content.

01:11:11.310 --> 01:11:13.560
A second problem that
we have is that there

01:11:13.560 --> 01:11:17.580
is tremendous distance between
the end user and the server.

01:11:17.580 --> 01:11:20.220
This costs money,
and it takes time

01:11:20.220 --> 01:11:24.480
to get content to the end user.

01:11:24.480 --> 01:11:27.900
Akamai Technologies-- Preetish--

01:11:27.900 --> 01:11:32.740
Akamai Technologies has a
breakthrough in this space.

01:11:32.740 --> 01:11:34.410
We have breakthrough
technologies

01:11:34.410 --> 01:11:37.260
that will allow ISPs to
host content at literally

01:11:37.260 --> 01:11:40.320
thousands, even hundreds
of thousands of locations

01:11:40.320 --> 01:11:43.500
worldwide with the
flip of a switch.

01:11:43.500 --> 01:11:46.980
In doing this, we will have
content that will always

01:11:46.980 --> 01:11:48.480
be close to the user.

01:11:48.480 --> 01:11:50.100
Intelligent replication
of the content

01:11:50.100 --> 01:11:52.350
will handle flash crowds.

01:11:52.350 --> 01:11:56.160
Content that the user
receives will always be fresh,

01:11:56.160 --> 01:11:58.410
and we've implemented these
technologies in such a way

01:11:58.410 --> 01:12:00.118
that they are transparent
to both the end

01:12:00.118 --> 01:12:02.610
user and the content
provider and that they

01:12:02.610 --> 01:12:04.620
will run on standard
inexpensive hardware.

01:12:08.160 --> 01:12:09.930
One of the things that
we've done in this

01:12:09.930 --> 01:12:13.470
is that we've introduced some
revolutionary technology that

01:12:13.470 --> 01:12:16.080
is the first step
in truly building

01:12:16.080 --> 01:12:19.320
an intelligent internet.

01:12:19.320 --> 01:12:21.360
Let's show you just a
couple of little examples

01:12:21.360 --> 01:12:25.080
of how we are going to make
this world of the internet

01:12:25.080 --> 01:12:27.400
a better world using
our technologies.

01:12:27.400 --> 01:12:29.480
The way the world looks
today as a user at CNN--

01:12:29.480 --> 01:12:32.310
a user somewhere over in
Europe anywhere in the world

01:12:32.310 --> 01:12:36.090
wants content from, for
example, cnn.com out of Atlanta.

01:12:36.090 --> 01:12:40.290
In order to get there, there is
a long and winding and terribly

01:12:40.290 --> 01:12:42.870
complex path that
they need to go by

01:12:42.870 --> 01:12:45.150
to get to the cnn.com site.

01:12:45.150 --> 01:12:47.820
The content needs to
travel a long distance

01:12:47.820 --> 01:12:51.530
through a complex network.

01:12:51.530 --> 01:12:59.400
What we propose through
the Akamai network

01:12:59.400 --> 01:13:01.470
is a distributed
series of servers

01:13:01.470 --> 01:13:05.730
that we have called global
hosting servers or ghosts.

01:13:05.730 --> 01:13:09.330
The name ghost is used
because these servers are

01:13:09.330 --> 01:13:12.270
invisible to the users, they
are invisible to the content

01:13:12.270 --> 01:13:15.480
providers, and they basically
perform this service

01:13:15.480 --> 01:13:17.370
of speeding up access
on the internet

01:13:17.370 --> 01:13:22.030
while being completely
invisible to all users.

01:13:22.030 --> 01:13:24.510
How does the network look
with these ghosts in place?

01:13:27.210 --> 01:13:30.810
A big mesh that gets built out
and looks terribly complex,

01:13:30.810 --> 01:13:33.507
but is easily understood
by these ghost servers.

01:13:33.507 --> 01:13:35.340
They have dynamic ways
of finding each other

01:13:35.340 --> 01:13:36.030
on the internet.

01:13:36.030 --> 01:13:38.280
They're completely fault
resistant, because it doesn't

01:13:38.280 --> 01:13:40.560
matter if one of them goes
down, the rest of them

01:13:40.560 --> 01:13:43.920
know how to find other
elements in this network.

01:13:43.920 --> 01:13:46.170
And what's going to happen
to the content from cnn.com

01:13:46.170 --> 01:13:49.470
is it will arrive
to the user from one

01:13:49.470 --> 01:13:51.410
of these closed
servers, not necessarily

01:13:51.410 --> 01:13:53.910
the closest, but certainly one
of the ones that's very, very

01:13:53.910 --> 01:13:56.460
close geographically.

01:13:56.460 --> 01:13:58.590
We do this in such
a way that we still

01:13:58.590 --> 01:14:03.960
allow the content provider that
is cnn.com to personalize pages

01:14:03.960 --> 01:14:06.942
and to know exactly who
arrived at their page.

01:14:06.942 --> 01:14:09.150
And this is something that
is unique to our solution,

01:14:09.150 --> 01:14:11.650
and it is something that content
providers have specifically

01:14:11.650 --> 01:14:16.070
asked us for in our
dialogues with them.

01:14:16.070 --> 01:14:17.820
That's a brief overview
of the technology,

01:14:17.820 --> 01:14:19.583
and I will hand off to Preetish.

01:14:19.583 --> 01:14:21.000
He will give you
some introduction

01:14:21.000 --> 01:14:22.404
to the market opportunity.

