01:33:42.510 --> 01:33:45.270
of Motorola Lexicus division,
which may remind you

01:33:45.270 --> 01:33:49.620
of the team that was also
in the competition in 1991,

01:33:49.620 --> 01:33:53.220
Lexicus Longhand was
his team, was recently

01:33:53.220 --> 01:33:54.090
bought by Motorola.

01:33:54.090 --> 01:33:55.650
And he is currently
working there.

01:33:55.650 --> 01:33:57.830
And he will--
well, of course, we

01:33:57.830 --> 01:34:00.240
must mention that he was
the fastest MIT alumni

01:34:00.240 --> 01:34:02.310
ever to make it to the
cover of Fortune Magazine

01:34:02.310 --> 01:34:03.210
after graduation.

01:34:03.210 --> 01:34:05.535
[APPLAUSE]

01:34:09.260 --> 01:34:10.840
Mr. Ronjon Nag.

01:34:10.840 --> 01:34:13.430
RONJON NAG: Thank you.

01:34:13.430 --> 01:34:15.440
This is a very exciting event.

01:34:15.440 --> 01:34:18.140
I'd just like to say a few
words for the people who

01:34:18.140 --> 01:34:20.240
haven't won today.

01:34:20.240 --> 01:34:22.040
I was one of probably
the equivalent

01:34:22.040 --> 01:34:24.380
of the 84 teams
in the first round

01:34:24.380 --> 01:34:26.640
who didn't even get
to the first round.

01:34:26.640 --> 01:34:29.330
And really, I'd like
to echo Bill's comment.

01:34:29.330 --> 01:34:35.690
It's really taking part can
generate so much enthusiasm

01:34:35.690 --> 01:34:37.370
for doing something more.

01:34:37.370 --> 01:34:39.990
And it's not just
winning, but taking part.

01:34:39.990 --> 01:34:42.200
But let's get to
the exciting part.

01:34:42.200 --> 01:34:45.680
It says here co
grand prize winner,

01:34:45.680 --> 01:34:49.235
and the team is Direct Hit.

01:34:49.235 --> 01:34:51.710
[APPLAUSE]

01:35:13.500 --> 01:35:16.630
GARY CULLISS: This is
absolutely amazing.

01:35:16.630 --> 01:35:19.360
I just want to say how
incredible this competition is

01:35:19.360 --> 01:35:20.020
it.

01:35:20.020 --> 01:35:21.990
We are here because
of the competition.

01:35:21.990 --> 01:35:24.250
We would have never
met each other.

01:35:24.250 --> 01:35:27.750
I am just-- I want to introduce
Steven Yang, one of the team

01:35:27.750 --> 01:35:30.920
members that you've heard a
little bit about already, David

01:35:30.920 --> 01:35:34.710
[? Doe, ?] also another
very valuable team member.

01:35:34.710 --> 01:35:36.300
And I just want to
thank everybody,

01:35:36.300 --> 01:35:37.471
all the lead organizers.

01:35:37.471 --> 01:35:38.263
This is incredible.

01:35:38.263 --> 01:35:39.229
Thank you.

01:35:39.229 --> 01:35:41.644
[APPLAUSE]

01:35:48.900 --> 01:35:50.470
MIKE CASSIDY: Wow.

01:35:50.470 --> 01:35:53.755
And I have one more small
surprise announcement, too.

01:35:53.755 --> 01:35:55.130
We have been
extremely fortunate.

01:35:55.130 --> 01:35:58.070
And between the time
we turned in our plan

01:35:58.070 --> 01:36:00.350
until tonight, we
actually had been

01:36:00.350 --> 01:36:04.190
approached by venture capitalist
and have achieved funding.

01:36:04.190 --> 01:36:06.260
Because that puts us
in a slight imposition,

01:36:06.260 --> 01:36:10.667
we have decided to give the
$30,000 to the other finalists.

01:36:10.667 --> 01:36:12.500
We'll split it up among
the other finalists.

01:36:12.500 --> 01:36:13.490
So thank you very much.

01:36:13.490 --> 01:36:15.985
[APPLAUSE]

01:36:42.530 --> 01:36:44.030
SCOTT BLANKSTEEN:
This was certainly

01:36:44.030 --> 01:36:46.187
an unpredictable evening.

01:36:46.187 --> 01:36:48.770
I don't think there was anyone
in the room who knew everything

01:36:48.770 --> 01:36:51.210
that was going to happen
at the end of this,

01:36:51.210 --> 01:36:53.930
including the judges.

01:36:53.930 --> 01:36:55.395
So here we are.

01:36:55.395 --> 01:36:57.770
First of all, let's, again,
just give our congratulations

01:36:57.770 --> 01:36:59.526
to everybody who
took part this year.

01:36:59.526 --> 01:37:02.502
[APPLAUSE]

01:37:09.960 --> 01:37:12.720
And to reward you for your
patience and your interest,

01:37:12.720 --> 01:37:14.970
we have some food afterwards,
some light refreshments,

01:37:14.970 --> 01:37:18.032
and a little time to mingle
and network a little more.

01:37:18.032 --> 01:37:20.490
Before we go, don't forget to
sign up for our mailing list,

01:37:20.490 --> 01:37:21.840
to keep in touch with
all the great stuff

01:37:21.840 --> 01:37:24.130
we'll be doing next year
on our 10th anniversary.

01:37:24.130 --> 01:37:26.680
And the final thought, maybe--

01:37:29.550 --> 01:37:30.450
goodnight.

01:37:30.450 --> 01:37:33.200
[APPLAUSE]

